 "poem": "The Spirit, who kept not them away,\nSaw the body of his son anyway,\nAnd blessed it and anointed he\nWith blood from his own mother's knee.\nXII. - The Death-Floor: The Dawn-Height He\nThat swoon'd to itself as finally\nHe lifted up her dead incarnation\nHis spirit wound like a maiden\nTo lift upon another tree.\nAnd with it all day long shortly\nOn earth a death-flower sprung consecrated,\nOf which on every day",
